.Im MicroEmacs modes
.so me.tni
.TH lf 2m
.XI lf - "File's line feed style"
.SH NAME
lf \- File's line feed style
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "lf Mode"
.sp
\fBl\fR \- mode line letter.
.SH DESCRIPTION
When  enabled  \fBlf\fR  indicates  that a line  feed  should be  written  out
including  the \fB\\n\fR  character.  When set then a \fB\\n\fR is included on
each line  ending.  When  clear then  \fB\\n\fR  is not  included  in the line
ending.
.SH NOTES
\fBlf\fR mode is used in conjunction with
.Ht cr 2m 
to control the carriage return, \fBlf\fR alone giving Unix and both Windows line endings.
.PP
When a file is read every carriage return (\fB\\r\fR), line feed (\fB\\n\fR) or carriage return and line feed ends a
line, each line keeping its own line ending, and the most common line ending sets the \fBcr\fR and \fBlf\fR modes.
A line whose ending differs from the modes is written with its own ending so the file is saved unchanged, see
.Ht $file-checks 5
for the check made when such a file is saved. Changing either mode gives every line the new line ending. A typed or
inserted line takes the buffer's line ending, see
.Ht insert-file 2 .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.na
